Wren preserves the upstream wire protocol verbatim - the SMART on FHIR session
relay endpoints and the ECDH P-256 + AES-256-GCM chunked end-to-end-encryption
scheme - so that the Tula `health-records` skill (skills/health-records/)
interoperates with a Wren backend without any code change, via the
`HEALTH_SKILLZ_BASE_URL` override.

RealActivity modifications:
  - Rebranding ("Health Skillz" -> "Wren").
  - A dark-first design-system reskin of the connection UI to match the
    RealActivity / my-aria visual language (OKLCH tokens, burgundy accent).
  - Packaging as the `services/wren` component of the Tula repository.

None of these modifications alter the wire protocol or the end-to-end
encryption posture. The server stores only ciphertext it cannot decrypt.

The full upstream MIT license text and copyright attribution are in LICENSE.
The original upstream README and agent notes are preserved verbatim as
UPSTREAM-README.md and UPSTREAM-AGENTS.md.

